🚀 **Project Highlight | Sentiment Analysis Using LSTM**

I’m pleased to share one of my recent **Natural Language Processing (NLP) projects: Sentiment Analysis using LSTM (Long Short-Term Memory)**.

🎯 **Objective**
Develop a Deep Learning model to analyze textual data and classify movie reviews based on sentiment. I used the **IMDb Movie Reviews Dataset**, which contains 50,000 labeled reviews.
🔍 **Key Technical Implementation**
• Performed text preprocessing and data preparation
• Applied **Tokenization and Sequence Padding**
• Built word representations using an **Embedding Layer**
• Designed an **LSTM-based neural network** for sequential text learning
• Used **Dropout layers** to help reduce overfitting
• Evaluated the model using classification and performance metrics

🏗️ **Model Architecture**
**Embedding → Dropout → LSTM → Dropout → Dense (Sigmoid)**

💡 **Key Takeaways**
This project strengthened my practical understanding of **NLP, Deep Learning, text preprocessing, sequence modeling, and LSTM architectures**. More importantly, it gave me hands-on experience in taking a real-world text classification problem from dataset preparation through model development and evaluation.

I’m actively building my portfolio in **Data Science, Machine Learning, NLP, and Generative AI**, and looking forward to applying these skills to real-world business problems.

